From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DarekM <149845949+aninmucek@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:42:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: zuma-akita: Add the touchscreen

The Pixel 8a's touchscreen is a Goodix GT9895 (Berlin) on USI2_HSI0's
SPI, the bus, interrupt and reset lines of the Pixel 8 Pro's: 10 MHz,
interrupt on gpn0-0 (falling edge, as stock's goodix,irq-flags = 2),
reset on gpp21-2 (Google's zuma-akita-touch.dtsi; the stock phone's
/proc/interrupts lists goodix_ts on gpn0 0 Edge). Both of stock's
firmware files, goodix_firmware_ak3a.bin and goodix_firmware_ak3b.bin,
carry "9895" in their Berlin header, so it takes the gt9895 match data
(14-byte contact records), as the Pixel 7a does. The driver runs the
firmware already on the chip and loads none.

The supplies are the LDO4M and LDO25M described with the PMIC, at
stock's 3.0 V and 1.8 V.

Tested on a Pixel 8a from slot B (7.3.0-rc6), in a later boot than the
one that first set the voltage: with the driver held back, the rails
read 3.0 V and 1.8 V and off; loading goodix_berlin_spi enabled them
and registered "Goodix Berlin Capacitive TouchScreen". Touches in the
four corners came in at (110,121), (1004,118), (118,2311) and
(971,2298), so no axis swap or inversion is needed, and 842 interrupts
gave no checksum errors. In the next boots the driver loads by itself,
and the PIN pad, the shell and the on-screen keyboard work by touch.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: DarekM <149845949+aninmucek@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-akita.dts     | 31 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-akita.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-akita.dts
index c7c1b3358..77cd6a350 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-akita.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zuma-akita.dts
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 
 #include <dt-bindings/gpio/gpio.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/input/input.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/interrupt-controller/irq.h>
 #include "zuma.dtsi"
 
 / {
@@ -146,6 +147,32 @@ touch_vdd: ldo25m {
 	};
 };
 
+&spi20 {
+	status = "okay";
+
+	/*
+	 * Goodix GT9895 (Berlin), the Pixel 7a's controller: both of stock's
+	 * firmware files (goodix_firmware_ak3a.bin and _ak3b.bin) say "9895".
+	 * Wired as zuma-husky's touchscreen: 10 MHz, interrupt on gpn0-0
+	 * (falling edge, stock's goodix,irq-flags = 2), reset on gpp21-2.
+	 * avdd is LDO4M at 3.0 V and vddio LDO25M at 1.8 V, as on stock.
+	 */
+	touchscreen@0 {
+		compatible = "goodix,gt9895";
+		reg = <0>;
+		spi-max-frequency = <10000000>;
+		interrupt-parent = <&gpn0>;
+		interrupts = <0 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_FALLING>;
+		reset-gpios = <&gpp21 2 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+		avdd-supply = <&touch_avdd>;
+		vddio-supply = <&touch_vdd>;
+		touchscreen-size-x = <1080>;
+		touchscreen-size-y = <2400>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+		pinctrl-0 = <&ts_irq &ts_reset>;
+	};
+};
+
 /*
  * Behind the init's storage guard (only slot B's boot images and userdata
  * writable), which sets every partition read-only before anything mounts
@@ -171,3 +198,7 @@ &usb_hsphy {
 &usbdrd_phy {
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+&usi2_hsi0 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
